tion hash and uses the epoch start time for the following week. This ensures that only\\n     * one proposal can be created per week.\\n     \"},\"state(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-state}.\\n     \"},\"proposalThreshold()\":{\"details\":\"Part of the Governor Bravo's interface: _\\\"The number of votes required in order for a voter to become a proposer\\\"_.\\n     \"},\"proposalSnapshot(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-proposalSnapshot}.\\n     \"},\"proposalDeadline(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-proposalDeadline}.\\n     \"},\"propose(uint256,address[],uint256[],bytes[],string)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-propose}.\\n     * description is ignored. The proposalId is created using the following epoch's start date.\\n     \"},\"execute(address[],uint256[],bytes[],bytes32)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-execute}.\\n     * Executes a proposal with a start time at the beginning of this epoch.\\n     \"},\"getVotes(address,uint256,uint256)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-getVotes}.\\n     \"},\"getVotesWithParams(address,uint256,uint256,bytes)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-getVotesWithParams}.\\n     \"},\"castVote(uint256,uint256,uint8)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-castVote}.\\n     \"},\"castVoteWithReason(uint256,uint256,uint8,string)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-castVoteWithReason}.\\n     \"},\"castVoteWithReasonAndParams(uint256,uint256,uint8,string,bytes)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-castVoteWithReasonAndParams}.\\n     \"},\"castVoteBySig(uint256,uint256,uint8,uint8,bytes32,bytes32)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-castVoteBySig}.\\n     \"},\"castVoteWithReasonAndParamsBySig(uint256,uint256,uint8,string,bytes,uint8,bytes32,bytes32)\":{\"details\":\"See {IGovernor-castVoteWithReasonAndParamsBySig}.\\n     \"},\"onERC721Received(address,address,uint256,bytes)\":{\"details\":\"See {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received}.\\n     \"},\"onERC1155Received(address,address,uint256,uint256,bytes)\":{\"details\":\"See {IERC1155Receiver-onERC1155Received}.\\n     \"},\"onERC1155BatchReceived(address,address,uint256[],uint256[],bytes)\":{\"details\":\"See {IERC1155Receiver-onERC1155BatchReceived}.\\n     \"},\"quorum(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Dummy quorum function to comply with IGovernor as quorum is not used.\\n     \"},\"clock()\":{\"details\":\"See {IERC6372}\\n     \"},\"CLOCK_MODE()\":{\"details\":\"See EIP-6372.\\n     \"},\"votingDelay()\":{\"details\":\"Delay, between the proposal is created and the vote starts. The unit this duration is expressed in depends\\n     * on the clock (see EIP-6372) this contract uses.\\n     *\\n     * This can be increased to leave time for users to buy voting power, or delegate it, before the voting of a\\n     * proposal starts.\\n     \"},\"votingPeriod()\":{\"details\":\"Delay, between the vote start and vote ends. The unit this duration is expressed in depends on the clock\\n     * (see EIP-6372) this contract uses.\\n     *\\n     * NOTE: The {votingDelay} can delay the start of the vote. This must be considered when setting the voting\\n     * duration compared to the voting delay.\\n     \"},\"eip712Domain()\":{\"details\":\"See {IERC-5267}.\\n     \"},\"trustedForwarder()\":{\"details\":\"Returns the address of the trusted forwarder.\\n     \"},\"isTrustedForwarder(address)\":{\"details\":\"Indicates whether any particular address is the trusted forwarder.\\n     \"}},\"details\":\"Modified lightly from OpenZeppelin's GovernorCountingSimple to support a simple three option majority.\\n *\\n \",\"events\":{\"ProposalCreated(uint256,address,address[],uint256[],string[],bytes[],uint256,uint256,string)\":{\"details\":\"Emitted when a proposal is created.\\n     \"},\"ProposalCanceled(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Emitted when a proposal is canceled.\\n     \"},\"ProposalExecuted(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Emitted when a proposal is executed.\\n     \"},\"VoteCast(address,uint256,uint256,uint8,uint256,string)\":{\"details\":\"Emitted when a vote is cast without params.\\n     *\\n     * Note: `support` values should be seen as buckets. Their interpretation depends on the voting module used.\\n     \"},\"VoteCastWithParams(address,uint256,uint256,uint8,uint256,string,bytes)\":{\"details\":\"Emitted when a vote is cast with params.\\n     *\\n     * Note: `support` values should be seen as buckets. Their interpretation depends on the voting module used.\\n     * `params` are additional encoded parameters. Their interpepretation also depends on the voting module used.\\n     \"},\"EIP712DomainChanged()\":{\"details\":\"MAY be emitted to signal that the domain could have changed.\\n     \"}},\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"result()\":{\"notice\":\"      Any contracts that wish to use this governor must read from this to determine results.\"},\"clock()\":{\"notice\":\"module:core\"},\"CLOCK_MODE()\":{\"notice\":\"module:core\"},\"votingDelay()\":{\"notice\":\"module:user-config\"},\"votingPeriod()\":{\"notice\":\"module:user-config\"}},\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"lib/crane/contracts/protocols/dexes/aerodrome/v1/stubs/governance/GovernorCountingMajority.sol\":\"GovernorCountingMajority\"},\"evmVersion\":\"osaka\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":1},\"remappings\":[\"@battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/src/\",\"@crane/=lib/crane/\",\"@matterlabs/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/lib/\",\"@nomicfoundation/=node_modules/@nomicfoundation/\",\"@opengsn/=node_modules/@opengsn/\",\"@openzeppelin/=node_modules/@openzeppelin/\",\"@oz/=lib/crane/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\"@ozu/=lib/crane/contracts/external/openzeppelin-upgradeable/\",\"battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/\",\"battlechain-lib-mocks/=lib/crane/lib/b